# Milestone: M3
# Covers: tag.stop() issued from one strand cancels a different strand that
#         is currently in WAITING state or mid-execution; the cancelled strand
#         does not produce further output.
#
# blocked: a chunk-top `,` group cannot share a declaration with its arms.
#          The fixture needs `var t = Tag.new()` visible to both the
#          tagged sleeper and the stopper, which means `;` before `,` --
#          and the parser refuses to mix the two in one group ("mixing ';'
#          and ',' in same group is ambiguous").  Probed: writing it all
#          with `,` makes every arm fail on `slot 't' not found`.
#          Cross-strand cancellation ITSELF works and is covered in C by
#          tests/rt/test_sched.c::stop_from_a_sibling_runs_the_finally.
#
# Everything below this line predates the re-foundation: it names
# tasks and entry points that no longer exist, and its account of
# what stands in the way has been superseded by the `blocked:` line
# above, which was probed against this branch.  Kept for the
# original urbiscript it carries.
# matrix-row: scheduler-strand
#
# Reason: cross-strand tag cancellation requires urbi_tag_stop's cross-strand
# deposit path (T31) which is not wired at M3.  At M3, tag.stop() only works
# synchronously within the same strand (when the unwind walker absorbs
# UEXEC_TAG_STOP in the cleanup stack, which itself lands at T29/T30).
# T39 is additionally needed for the ## host: mechanism to drive two strands
# in a chk fixture.
#
# When T31 + T39 land, implement this fixture by:
#   ## host: create strand A (blocking body); create strand B (calls tag.stop on A's tag)
#   ## host: start A and B; step until quiescent
#   ## host: assert A produced no output after the stop point
